<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tihosuco</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tihosuco is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quintana-roo">Quintana Roo</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, in the east of the Yucatán peninsula, which was a colonial parish centre on the frontier of Spanish settlement. Jacinto Pat, one of the leaders of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caste-war-of-yucatan">Caste War of Yucatán</a>, was its Maya headman, and the town was largely abandoned during the war after 1847, its church partly destroyed. It now houses a museum of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caste">Caste</a> War.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tihosuco.jpg" alt="Tihosuco" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Guillermo Isaac Huesca Solis · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tihosuco.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
